// Replacing a row of a rank-2 array.
//
// shc used to die with SIGSEGV and no diagnostic on the two shapes at
// the bottom of this case. The checker typed the right-hand side only
// when it was an array literal and returned without typing it
// otherwise, so every name in it stayed unresolved and the generator
// read a null symbol. Replacing a row from a LITERAL was fine, which is
// the form SHALIMAR_LANGUAGE.md section 9 gives as its example - so the
// documented spelling worked and the other two killed the compiler.
//
// Nothing was wrong with the generator: it has emitted shm_set_ref for
// an array element all along, and was simply never handed a typed
// expression to emit.
fun <> = main() {
  real A[2][5]
  real m[2][3]
  real r[3]
  int i

  // the documented form, from a literal
  A[0] : {1.,2.}
  ? A[0].row

  for i : 0 to 2 {
    r[i] : (i + 1) * 1.5
  }

  // from an array variable
  m[1] : r
  ? m[1][0] m[1][1] m[1][2]

  // from another row
  m[0] : m[1]
  ? m[0][0] m[0][2]

  // and the row still measures itself
  ? m[0].row

  return
}
